Add "go ... searchmoves <moves>" to hivemind's UCI interface.

The root may then only play the given moves (board-prefixed like the position
command, all on one board), with the other board still free. The site's game
review uses it to value the move a player actually chose with a search of the
same position, team and TimeAdvantage setting as the engine's best move.
The root mate scans, mate probe and certification veto are switched off for a
restricted search, and its tree is never reused.

engine/build.sh applies this on top of HIVEMIND_COMMIT.

